  "selection_rule": "Each configuration is fitted on the training window and scored on the validation window [validation_start, test_start) of every task, for every seed, by the per-period Sharpe ratio of the fitted policy simulated there with the task's costs. Scores are averaged over seeds, ranked within each task (the best of N configurations gets rank N, ties share the mean rank), and the single configuration with the highest mean rank across tasks is selected; remaining ties go to the earliest declared configuration. Test sessions are never loaded by the search.",
  "rationale": "Learning rate: the SB3 default 3e-4 against 1e-3; daily-return rewards are noisy, so the question is whether faster learning finds better policies within the fixed timestep budget. Network width: the default [64, 64] against [128, 128], to test whether more capacity helps on 8-10 asset features or only overfits. Horizon: 252-session episodes with gamma 0.99 (default; effective horizon about 100 sessions) against 63-session (one quarter) episodes with gamma 0.95 (effective horizon about 20 sessions), because the reward is a per-session log return and a shorter credit horizon reduces variance. Timesteps, features, reward and checkpoint selection are held at the base submission's values. The grid is the full 2 x 2 x 2 factorial and includes the untuned default. Note: SB3Policy itself keeps the checkpoint with the best validation Sharpe, so every configuration's validation score is an optimistic, checkpoint-selected number; the bias is the same for all configurations and the leaderboard's deflation uses trials = 8.",
